  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to possess, to have",
      "explanation": "A formal verb meaning to possess or be endowed with something. Used in written language, official documents, and formal descriptions rather than everyday conversation."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "13400_yuusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "この{地域|ちいき}は{豊|ゆた}かな{資源|しげん}を{有|ゆう}する。",
      "english": "This region possesses abundant resources.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13400_yuusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{長年|ながねん}の{経験|けいけん}を{有|ゆう}する{専門家|せんもんか}だ。",
      "english": "He is a specialist with many years of experience.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13400_yuusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{当社|とうしゃ}は{国内|こくない}に{百|ひゃく}を{超|こ}える{店舗|てんぽ}を{有|ゆう}しており、{全国|ぜんこく}で{展開|てんかい}している。",
      "english": "Our company possesses over a hundred stores domestically and operates nationwide.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). No intransitive pair.\n\nREGISTER:\nA formal, literary verb. In everyday speech and writing, {持|も}つ or {持|も}っている is used instead. {有|ゆう}する appears in legal texts, academic writing, company profiles, and news articles.\n\nCONJUGATION:\nThis is a する verb. Conjugates as {有|ゆう}する → {有|ゆう}して → {有|ゆう}した → {有|ゆう}しない.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {権利|けんり}を{有|ゆう}する: to hold a right\n- {資格|しかく}を{有|ゆう}する: to hold a qualification\n- {能力|のうりょく}を{有|ゆう}する: to possess ability\n- {歴史|れきし}を{有|ゆう}する: to have a history",
